ngl Print: say each character of a string
Print(w, next) vs Nil        => next ~ w
Print(w, next) vs Cons[c](s) => Say[c](w2) ~ w, s ~ Print(w2, next)

ngl Show: spell a number's digits, then Print them
ngl Spell counts on n <= 0 so INT64_MIN still works
Show(w, next) vs n
  if n < 0 => Say['-'](w2) ~ w, n ~ Spell(w2, next, Nil)
  else     => 0 - n ~ Spell(w, next, Nil)
Spell(w, next, s) vs n
  if n > -10 => Cons['0' - n](s) ~ Print(w, next)
  else       => n / 10 ~ Spell(w, next, Cons['0' - n % 10](s))

ngl Math: `a ~ Add(r, b)` puts a + b on r
Add(r, y) vs n     => y ~ AddWith[n](r)
AddWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a + b
Sub(r, y) vs n     => y ~ SubWith[n](r)
SubWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a - b
Mul(r, y) vs n     => y ~ MulWith[n](r)
MulWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a * b
Div(r, y) vs n     => y ~ DivWith[n](r)
DivWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a / b
Mod(r, y) vs n     => y ~ ModWith[n](r)
ModWith[a](r) vs b => r ~ a % b
Eq(r, y) vs n      => y ~ EqWith[n](r)
EqWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a == b
Lt(r, y) vs n      => y ~ LtWith[n](r)
LtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a < b
Gt(r, y) vs n      => y ~ GtWith[n](r)
GtWith[a](r) vs b  => r ~ a > b